course: dictionary
lesson: 3665
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word fit has several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a size, a body, a sudden attack, or whether something is suitable. «To spot sarcasm, check whether the words fit the situation and the tone.» Here fit means match or suit, so the words must go well with what is happening.
explain: «Shoes that fit are the right size for your feet.» Here fit means the right size and shape. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the right size for your feet" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Fit can also mean healthy and strong, as in «keep fit». A fit can also be a sudden short attack, like a fit of coughing or giggles. The spelling stays the same, so read the words around fit to find its meaning.
fact: Fit can be a verb, an adjective or a noun.
fact: As a verb, fit means to be the right size and shape to go in a place, or to put something in place.
fact: As an adjective, fit means healthy and strong, or right and good enough for something.
fact: As a noun, a fit is a sudden short attack, like a fit of coughing or giggles. «Fit in» means to belong with a group.
fact: In maths, to find how many boxes you need, divide the total by how many fit in each box. If there are leftovers, round up.
exercise: «The shoes did not fit, so Ella took them back.» What does fit mean here? | A sudden short attack | To be healthy and strong | To be very tired | *To be the right size for your feet
exercise: Dad says, «I want to keep fit this year.» What does fit mean here? | The right size for a box | *Healthy and strong | A sudden short attack | Very loud
exercise: Ben had a fit of giggles in class. What is a fit in this sentence? | A healthy body | *A sudden short attack | A kind of exercise | The right size for a box
test: How many boxes do you need if 6 cakes fit in each box and you have 25 cakes? | 25 | *5 | 6 | 4
test: «To spot sarcasm, check whether the words fit the situation.» What does fit mean here? | Put in a box | Keep healthy | A sudden attack | *Match or suit
exam: Which sentence uses fit to mean a sudden short attack? | «The team will fit in the bus.» | «She likes to keep fit by running.» | «The shoes fit well.» | *«He had a fit of coughing in class.»
